    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Does your pet dog "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tilt",
            "zh": "倾斜"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " its head when hearing its name? If the answer is yes, congratulations! That dog may be a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "genius",
            "ref": "v-genius"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A new study found that the head tilt isn’t a sign of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "confusion",
            "ref": "v-confusion"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", as many of us may believe. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", it’s actually a sign that the dog is "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "processing",
            "ref": "v-process"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the meaning of words. Dogs that tilted their heads most often in the study were also the best performing at responding to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "commands",
            "zh": "响应命令"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Dr Andrea Sommese, a researcher at the Eötvös Loránd University in Budapest, is the lead author of the study. He was inspired to conduct this research after taking part in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Genius Dog Challenge"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". In this "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "live broadcasted",
            "zh": "现场直播的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " series, very "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " dogs competed against each other. During the broadcasts, some of the dogs were very "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " learning the names of different kinds of toys."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Sommese and other researchers carefully "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "analysed",
            "ref": "v-analyse"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " all the broadcasts from the series. The owners were asked to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their pets the names of two toys. They would then test the dogs’ performance on the task once a month for 3 months. The test was simple. The dog had to fetch the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " toy when its name was said by the owner."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Most of the dogs "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at this task, although they were known to be smart "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "breeds",
            "zh": "品种"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Even two toy names proved to be too much for them. However, all seven "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "border collies",
            "zh": "边境牧羊犬"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " passed the test "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Throughout the experiment, the scientists recorded whether the dogs tilted their heads when their owners called out the toy’s name. The result was "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The gifted learners tilted their heads 43% of the time, while the other 33 dogs did so just 2% of the time. That doesn’t sound like a coincidence."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "So do these findings "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " your dog is not very smart if it’s not tilting its head? Not really."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“What we tested is a very "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "specific",
            "ref": "v-specific"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ": the ability to learn object names,” says Shany Dror, co-author of the study. “All dogs, however, are good at understanding their humans. They are "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "fine-tuned",
            "zh": "调整到最佳状态的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to all our activities and can learn a lot by "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "observing",
            "ref": "v-observe"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " us.”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
